IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `we57-nouns`
IMPORT `we57-cross-references`

-- Row il-57. The three controls hold, and the recorded facts about the three items are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their five failing assertions are in we57-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in we57-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound controls`

-- Control 1: the cumulation rule names (ד3), points at what it says, and is complete both before and after Amendment 67 takes effect.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: the cumulation rule in s 6(ד2), which names (ד3)`)
#ASSERT `the citing words are complete on` (`reference: the cumulation rule in s 6(ד2), which names (ד3)`) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the citing words are complete on` (`reference: the cumulation rule in s 6(ד2), which names (ד3)`) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the citing words are complete on` (`reference: the cumulation rule in s 6(ד2), which names (ד3)`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Control 2: the new (א3) cites a section that exists as Amendment 67 inserts it, and names itself.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 51(א3), which cites s 6(ד3) of the Law`)
#ASSERT `the citing words are complete on` (`reference: s 51(א3), which cites s 6(ד3) of the Law`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Control 3: the National Insurance Law's replacement says the masculine form under a masculine noun, and the pronoun fits every noun its head names.
#ASSERT `the pronoun fits every noun the head names` (`pronoun: the five-day limb in the National Insurance Law's definition, as the same instrument replaces the words`)
#ASSERT (`pronoun: the five-day limb in the National Insurance Law's definition, as the same instrument replaces the words`)'s `the gender of the pronoun and its verb` EQUALS `masculine`

§ `Tests of what the recorded values say about item 1 (the list of extensions)`

-- The descriptions of the definition: the citing words list three subsections, the target has four.
#ASSERT (`reference: the definition of the extensions in s 6(ב)(2)`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the extensions under sections 6(ב1), (ג) and (ד) of the Law`
#ASSERT (`reference: the definition of the extensions in s 6(ב)(2)`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `the extensions under sections 6(ב1), (ג), (ד) and (ד3) of the Law`
#ASSERT NOT (`reference: the definition of the extensions in s 6(ב)(2)`)'s `the citing words name that subsection`
-- The gap opens on the day Amendment 67 is read to take effect (the builder's computation, fork D1): before it nothing is missing, from it the subsection is not named.
#ASSERT `the citing words are complete on` (`reference: the definition of the extensions in s 6(ב)(2)`) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the citing words are complete on` (`reference: the definition of the extensions in s 6(ב)(2)`) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The dependants take the definition's description, and carry no claim of their own.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 6(ח)(1א), which uses the defined term`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS (`reference: the definition of the extensions in s 6(ב)(2)`)'s `the citing words say it points at`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 7(ד)(1), which uses the defined term`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS (`reference: the definition of the extensions in s 6(ב)(2)`)'s `the citing words say it points at`
-- The two other lists name three or more subsections and not (ד3); that they should is a policy question this row does not answer (fork R3), so only what they print is asserted.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: the list in s 6(ז1)(2)`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: the list in s 9ג(ב)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reference: the list in s 6(ז1)(2)`)'s `the citing words name that subsection`
#ASSERT NOT (`reference: the list in s 9ג(ב)`)'s `the citing words name that subsection`

§ `Tests of what the recorded values say about item 2 (section 51(ד))`

#ASSERT (`reference: s 51(ד) of the National Insurance Law`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the payment date of the additional maternity allowance under section 51(א) and (א1) of the National Insurance Law`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 51(ד) of the National Insurance Law`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `the payment date of the additional maternity allowance under section 51(א), (א1) and (א3) of the National Insurance Law`
#ASSERT NOT (`reference: s 51(ד) of the National Insurance Law`)'s `the citing words name that subsection`
#ASSERT `the citing words are complete on` (`reference: s 51(ד) of the National Insurance Law`) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the citing words are complete on` (`reference: s 51(ד) of the National Insurance Law`) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests of what the recorded values say about item 3 (the pronoun)`

-- The paragraph's head names a man and a woman; the pronoun and its verb are feminine.
#ASSERT (`pronoun: the five-day limb in the Law, as the 2026 instrument replaces the words`)'s `the gender of the pronoun and its verb` EQUALS `feminine`
#ASSERT `some gender in the list is` `masculine` ((`pronoun: the five-day limb in the Law, as the 2026 instrument replaces the words`)'s `the nouns the head of the paragraph names`)
#ASSERT `some gender in the list is` `feminine` ((`pronoun: the five-day limb in the Law, as the 2026 instrument replaces the words`)'s `the nouns the head of the paragraph names`)
-- The pronoun does fit one noun the head names (the feminine one), so the limb is not unreadable; what fails is fitting every noun (in the red file).
#ASSERT `the pronoun fits some noun the head names` (`pronoun: the five-day limb in the Law, as the 2026 instrument replaces the words`)

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- No reference in the three items has both limbs read from the official instruments alone, except the National Insurance control whose both limbs are the one instrument.
#ASSERT NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: the definition of the extensions in s 6(ב)(2)`)
#ASSERT NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: the cumulation rule in s 6(ד2), which names (ד3)`)
#ASSERT NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 51(ד) of the National Insurance Law`)
#ASSERT NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 51(א3), which cites s 6(ד3) of the Law`)
-- Limb (a) of the defects is the consolidation only; limb (b) carries the caveat that no later instrument is known to have touched the words only because the consolidation prints them unchanged.
#ASSERT (`reference: the definition of the extensions in s 6(ב)(2)`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: the definition of the extensions in s 6(ב)(2)`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 51(ד) of the National Insurance Law`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 51(ד) of the National Insurance Law`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`pronoun: the five-day limb in the Law, as the 2026 instrument replaces the words`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`pronoun: the five-day limb in the National Insurance Law's definition, as the same instrument replaces the words`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
